From ec0ba00340085dc8cfe989a42c817e9d24ba544d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/43] usb_webcam: add a YUY2 conversion for UVC and its tests

UVC cameras send uncompressed video as YUY2. The UVC add-on treats
it as a Bayer pattern, which gives wrong colours. UVCColor.h converts
YUY2 (limited range, BT.601) to B_RGB32 and tells whether a frame
holds a whole picture. It needs no camera, so it can be tested on
its own. The next commit uses it.

UVCColorTest pins the conversion down; UVCColorBenchmark measures it
(0.95 ms for 640x480 on an i7-7500U).

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 00ff152d03991485c6271152f4cb22d5bc775eb1)
